/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * creep
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * creep(motor, sw)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to use
 * (>) sw (int)             Switch to creep into
 * (>) d (int)              Distance to creep (on either side of switch)
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Creep into a switch position
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Move very slowly into a switch so as to get a precise measure of when
 * the switch trips, in order to determine if motor steps have been
 * lost.  The OMS controller doesn't allow this for the HOME switch; if
 * you go to home via the internal controls, the switch reading is
 * reset.  If 'd' is zero, position 10 steps before the nominal
 * switch position, and creep from there at most 20 steps.  If 'd' is
 * not zero, replace 10/20 with d/2d.
 *
 * This routine is primarily for checking the home switch.  It can be
 * used for a positive limit switch, but not for a negative one since
 * (at least in principle) there's no way to remove the backlash without
 * moving though the switch and approaching from the "wrong" direction.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * useAlt
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * useAlt(motor, flag)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to use
 * (>) flag (BOOL)          Use alternative switch if non-zero
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (void) Returns 'void' and hence has no STATUS value
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Activate/deactivate alternative home switch
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Set hardware and software to use alternative home switch if flag
 * is true; otherwise, use primary switch.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * homeOffset
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * homeOffset(motor)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)          Motor to use
 * (>) d (int)              Distance to creep (on either side of switch)
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (void) Returns 'void' and hence has no STATUS value
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Determine home switch offset.
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Determines position of both home switches and in the process both
 * verifies that the switches are offset approximately as described
 * in the configuration file, and prints out the measured offset.
 *
 * Parameter 'd' is passed to the 'creep' routine, and can be omitted
 * at the command line to pass 0 (ie, use the internal default).
 *
 * Leaves the system configured with the primary home switch in use.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
