/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * moveAll
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * moveAll()
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * None
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Move all motors to new positions
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Assumes that each motor has been "marked" by having a new position
 * and associated command stored in the motor structure (see datumMech(),
 * setPostionReq(), etc in commands.c).  Computes the position of the
 * focus motor based on the new position, then calls doAll() to move
 * the motors.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * doAll
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * doAll()
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * None
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Move all the motors
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Moves all the motors to their new positions without being
 * concerned about the focus motor (see moveAll).
 *
 * EPICS uses the moveMech(), moveOneMotor API; moveAll and doAll are
 * for debugging convenience.  Note that the semGive in doAll releases
 * a task associated with that motor, and this in turn calls moveOneMotor.
 * It is in that function that the EPICS and command line call
 * sequence converge.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
