/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * sysinfo
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * sysinfo(which)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) which (int)          multifaceted input parameter (see below)
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (void) Returns 'void' and hence has no STATUS value
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Print a lot of system information
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Print out a lot of system info based on the 'which' argument:
 *   0      print everything
 *   1-n    print only section n
 *   nn     if two digit, then print subsection of section n
 *          (ie, which == 23, print section 2, item 3)
 *   nnn    same as nn but for sections with items numbered 10 and above
 *   n99    Print all sections up to and including 'n'.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * hrtest
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * hrtest(motor)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) motor (int)
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Test the home sense mechanism
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Issue an HR command which will send the motor to home ASSUMING
 * it's on the positive (switch not depressed) side of the cam.
 * If there's noise on the home line and this is issued several
 * times, the motor may stop shy of the home position upon a false
 * home transition.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * dohrtest
 *
 * INVOCATION:
